## 🟡 LOW — Settings "re-handshake on VID/PID change" runs on the UI thread (tray freeze)

When the Windows/Linux settings dialog saves a changed VID/PID, it synchronously re-runs the handshake **on the dialog's own message-loop thread**:
- `src/tray.rs:1002-1003` (Windows) and `src/linux_tray.rs:740-741` (and the Windows window-info picker at `src/tray.rs:1930-1931`)

`perform_handshake` can block for up to the **`CALLBACK_SWEEP_DEADLINE` of 5 s** (`src/core/notifier.rs`) on a misbehaving board, plus the per-`QUERY_CALLBACK` retry budget. That freezes the tray/menu-bar UI for seconds right after clicking OK. (The poll thread's own `perform_handshake` is on a background thread; this path isn't.)

**Fix:** spawn the reset+handshake onto a worker thread (the way the tray already does for `edit_rules`), or at minimum document that the dialog may briefly hang.

