## 🟡 LOW — Windows drops every window whose title is a single character

`src/platforms/windows.rs:308`:
```rust
if window_info.title.chars().count() < 2 && !window_info.title.is_empty() {
    return true; // ignored
}
```
The PRD's window-filtering spec (§7 / `PLATFORMS.md §1.4`) only calls for filtering *internal/shell* windows (`Shell_TrayWnd`, `ApplicationFrameWindow`, tray flyouts). A blanket drop of all 1-character titles is an undocumented heuristic — any legit app/game/tool with a 1-char title (e.g. a single glyph, or a terminal showing one character) is silently never reported to the keyboard, so a host rule for it would never fire. It's marked "Bug 5" in a comment but the behavior is aggressive. Worth at least surfacing in the Show-Window-Information list (currently those windows are hidden too) or relaxing to known-shell-only.

---

## ⚪ INFO — macOS title lookup can yield empty titles for some apps

`src/platforms/macos.rs::get_active_window_info` pairs the frontmost app's `localizedName` with a window by requiring `kCGWindowOwnerName == localizedName`. These two strings are usually equal but **not guaranteed** (bundle/exec-name vs. display-name divergence in some Electron/helper apps). When they differ, no window matches and `title` stays empty — title-pattern host rules (`["*chrome*","*youtube*"]`) silently never match for that app. Not a regression, but worth a fallback (e.g. match by window layer/owner PID, or fall back to `WM_NAME`-equivalent).

---

## ⚪ INFO — `--config` is ambiguous (no `--reload`)

`src/main.rs`: `qmkonnect --config <path>` (without `-r`) is intercepted by the `-c/--config` create-config branch and **silently ignores `<path>`**, creating a default config instead of using the supplied one. `--help` documents `--config <path>` only as a `--reload` companion, but the bare form parses and misleads. Minor UX trap.

---

### Summary

| # | Severity | Area | One-liner |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 🔴 HIGH | Packaging (Linux) | XDG autostart + globally-enabled systemd user service = **two daemons** at login, no single-instance guard → duplicate HID writes |
| 2 | 🟠 MED | Hyprland | `poll_window_state` holds focus lock across `notify_qmk` HID I/O (violates the invariant every sibling obeys) |
| 3 | 🟡 LOW | Tray (Win/Linux) | Re-handshake on VID/PID change runs on the UI thread → up to 5 s tray freeze |
| 4 | 🟡 LOW | Windows | 1-character-title windows are silently dropped (beyond the PRD's shell-filter spec) |
| 5 | ⚪ INFO | macOS | Title pairing via `owner==localizedName` can miss some apps |
| 6 | ⚪ INFO | CLI | `--config <path>` without `--reload` silently ignores the path |

The **#1 finding is the one I'd fix before any beta release** — it affects the headline Linux installers (.deb/.rpm/AUR) on the primary target distros and produces visibly wrong behavior (double keymap switches) for every systemd-Linux user. Want me to write the fix for #1 (single-instance guard on Linux + the `.desktop` condition) or #2 (release-the-lock-before-notify in `poll_window_state`)?
